                                <%# 2026-11-20 (John): slide / rotate TIME MODEL for planned wells — sources = saved Slide Sheets of offsets or LAS files %>
                                <details id="srmPanel" class="mb-2" style="border:1px solid var(--an-border,#1e2d3d);border-radius:6px;padding:6px 10px;">
                                    <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;">⏱ Time model for planned wells — slide / rotate from offsets <span id="srmBadge" style="font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080)"></span></summary>
                                    <div style="padding-top:8px;font-size:12px;">
                                        <div class="dmk-bar">
                                            <label>Time model <select id="srmActive" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="display:inline-block;width:auto"><option value="0">Single ROP (Pason ROP plot)</option><option value="1">Slide / rotate (offset model)</option></select></label>
                                            <label>Offsets (MTX IDs) <input id="srmIds" class="form-control form-control-sm" placeholder="auto: same Area" style="display:inline-block;width:150px"></label>
                                            <button type="button" id="srmLoadBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info">Load saved Slide Sheets</button>
                                            <label class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-warning" style="margin:0">⬆ Upload LAS (EDR, 1 s)<input type="file" id="srmLas" accept=".las,.LAS,.txt" multiple style="display:none"></label>
                                            <% if (user.role !== 'viewer') { %><button type="button" id="srmSaveBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-success">💾 Save model to job</button><% } %>
                                            <span id="srmStatus" style="color:#00c8ff;"></span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div id="srmSources"></div>
                                        <div id="srmModelTbl"></div>
                                        <div style="font-size:10.5px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-top:4px;">
                                            Per section (Surface 0→SC, Build SC→IC, Lateral IC→TD): slide % = slid m ÷ drilled m; ROP slide / rotate = metres ÷ on-bottom time of the EDR intervals of that mode;
                                            time = slid m ÷ ROP slide + rotated m ÷ ROP rotate (effective ROP = 1 ÷ (f ÷ ROP slide + (1−f) ÷ ROP rotate)). Pooled over the ticked sources; the Min / Avg / Max selector picks the slowest source / pooled / fastest source.
                                            Saved Slide Sheets use their own well's casing comments for the sections; LAS files use the sections of the well selected in Drilling Mechanics (same pad design assumed).
                                            Slide / rotate detection of LAS files: same rules and defaults as the Slide Sheet page. On-bottom time only (no connections / surveys); the milestone pauses are added on top.
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </details>
                                <div id="pasonPlotsViewer" style="display:none;">
                                    <%# 2026-11-20 (John): KPIs per hole section (from the trajectory milestones of the selected well) above the plots;
                                         curve Min / Avg / Max of the Pason export, default Min, saved per user (MTXPrefs key dmKpiCurve). %>
                                    <style>
                                        .dmk-bar{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px; align-items:center; margin-bottom:8px; font-size:12px; color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8); }
                                        .dmk-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); gap:10px; margin-bottom:12px; }
                                        .dmk-sec{ border:1px solid var(--an-border,#1e2d3d); border-radius:6px; padding:8px 10px; background:var(--an-panel,#111820); }
                                        .dmk-sec h6{ margin:0 0 6px; font-size:14px; color:var(--an-text-bright,#e8f4ff); }
                                        .dmk-sec h6 span{ font-size:11px; color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080); font-weight:400; }
                                        .dmk-cards{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:6px; }
                                        .dmk-c{ border:1px solid var(--an-border,#1e2d3d); border-radius:4px; padding:5px 6px; text-align:center; }
                                        .dmk-c .l{ font-size:10px; letter-spacing:1px; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080); }
                                        .dmk-c .v{ font-size:17px; font-weight:700; font-family:var(--an-mono,monospace); }
                                        .dmk-c .u{ font-size:10px; color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080); }
                                        .dmk-c.rop{ cursor:pointer; } .dmk-c.rop:hover{ border-color:#00e5ff; }
                                        .dmk-flag{ font-size:12px; margin-top:6px; } .dmk-flag.bad{ color:#ffb020; } .dmk-flag.ok{ color:#39ff14; }
                                        .dmk-off{ font-size:12px; margin-top:4px; color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8); }
                                        @media (max-width:700px){ .dmk-cards{ grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); } .dmk-c .v{ font-size:18px; } }
                                    </style>
                                    <div class="dmk-bar">
                                        <b>KPIs per section</b>
                                        <label>Well <select id="dmkWell" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="display:inline-block;width:auto;"></select></label>
                                        <label>Curve <select id="dmkCurve" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="display:inline-block;width:auto;" title="Which Pason curve the KPIs use. Saved for your user.">
